                <item>
                <title><![CDATA[【Unreleased/Unofficial (lossless)】WAV - Willa Ford - (Not Such an) Innocent Girl | Later Recorded by Victoria Beckham]]></title>
                <link><![CDATA[https://sharemania.us/threads/willa-ford-not-such-an-innocent-girl-later-recorded-by-victoria-beckham.293090/]]></link>
                <description><![CDATA[<article>
				<blockquote class="messageText SelectQuoteContainer ugc baseHtml">
					
					<div style="text-align: center"><br>
<img src="https://i.imgur.com/qD2YlAS.jpeg" class="bbCodeImage LbImage" alt="[​IMG]" data-url="https://i.imgur.com/qD2YlAS.jpeg" style="">​</div><br>
As Victoria Beckham experiences a surprise uptick of her 2001 single on iTunes, I decided it would be nice to share the original take.<br>
<br>
Pop lore has it that "<b>Innocent Girl</b>" (the "Not Such an" bit was added later) was first offered to <b>Willa Ford</b> for her 2001 album, <i><b>Willa Was Here</b></i>. A YouTube search will take you to an infamous live performance of the song before the album dropped -- however, it didn't make the final cut.<br>
<br>
It was alleged to then be held over for her follow-up<i><b>, Porn Poetry</b></i> (later renamed<b><i> SexySexObsessive</i></b>), but that album was shelved.<br>
<br>
A few years ago, pop fans received a grail in the form of Willa's original version. No word on if she was compensated for Victoria maintaining the same vocal style. <img src="styles/default/xenforo/clear.png" class="mceSmilieSprite mceSmilie49" alt=":grimacing:" title="Grimacing    :grimacing:"><img src="styles/default/xenforo/clear.png" class="mceSmilieSprite mceSmilie49" alt=":grimacing:" title="Grimacing    :grimacing:"><img src="styles/default/xenforo/clear.png" class="mceSmilieSprite mceSmilie49" alt=":grimacing:" title="Grimacing    :grimacing:"><br>
<br>
<span style="text-decoration: underline"><b>Personal note</b></span>: I've had these versions for some time in this format. I'm unaware if they are pure or altered files.<br>
<br>
As a fan of both Willa's and Victoria's, I'm sharing this for others to enjoy a version of a pop gem they may not be familiar with. Please be kind and enjoy.<br>
<br>
